enchilada: battery: SOC, capacities, cycles, V/I/T from the bq27541 fuel gauge on SE10, read only

0275 showed a voltage-derived estimate (about +-10 points). The OnePlus 6 gauge is a TI bq27541 at
0x55 on QUPv3 SE10 (dtbo board 17819 fragment@71 "ti,bq27541-battery" on qupv3_se10_i2c =
i2c@a88000, 100 kHz; fg-gen3 has oem,use_external_fg; mainline sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi lists
it as "ti,bq27411" on i2c10). sweet_touch.c's GENI FIFO I2C core now takes a per-SE state (touch
keeps its globals through touch_msg()/touch_read() wrappers; fajita_clocks() takes the SE's vote
mask, CBCR and RCG; the 0x5200c vote RMW is under one mutex) and gains sweet_bq_read(): SE10 =
wrapper 1 SE2, gcc_qupv3_wrap1_s2_clk vote bit 24 + m/s AHB bits 20/21, CBCR 0x18274, RCG
0x18278 to XO/1 (gcc-sdm845.c, the same sequence SE12 touch uses); gpio55/56 NORTH function qup10,
switched only if not already qup10 (Linux applies qupv3_se10_i2c_active: qup10, 2 mA, no bias);
pin and clock state logged. Every gauge transfer is a 1-byte register-pointer write plus a
repeated-START 2-byte read of a standard command; no Control() subcommand, no data flash, no other
address. SweetBattery (PMI8998 path only, from the work loop, first access at the first full poll)
picks the register map by plausibility (bq27541 06/08/2c vs bq27411 02/04/1c: V 3000-4500 mV,
T -40..100 C, SOC <= 100, exactly one must match; raw words logged once), then every 30 s reads
Temperature, Voltage, Flags, AverageCurrent, StateOfCharge, FullChargeCapacity,
RemainingCapacity, CycleCount and once DesignCapacity (0x3c). iOS gets SOC (clamped 1-100) via
CurrentCapacity/MaxCapacity = FCC, AppleRawCurrentCapacity = RM, AppleRawMaxCapacity = FCC,
DesignCapacity = DCAP (1000-10000, else 3300), CycleCount, gauge V/I, temperature clamped 0-45 C;
IsCharging/ExternalConnected/FullyCharged stay PMI8998 SMB2. Errors back off 1, 2, 4 .. 32 polls,
the last good sample is held 5 minutes, then the 0275 estimate (still published as
SweetBatteryVEstimate) is used; SE10 setup failure disables the gauge for the boot. Logs:
"SWEET BATT SE10:" pin/clock/SE lines, "SWEET BATT: bq27541 at SE10 0x55: SOC .. FCC .. RM ..
cycles .. V .. I .. T .." once, failures rate-limited. No boot-arg; sweetbattery=0 still forces the
static source.

